---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---
<Page title="Privacy" description="What this site records about visitors: cookieless page-view counts only. No cookies, no ads, no tracking across sites, nothing sold.">
  <section class="intro"><h1>Privacy</h1></section>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Short version: this site sets no cookies and doesn't know who you are.</p>
    <h2>What is recorded</h2>
    <p>
      To see whether anyone reads this, two cookieless tools count visits:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>My own counter</strong>, running on Cloudflare. It stores the page
        path, the referring site (if it's another site), how far down the page you
        scrolled, which links or buttons you clicked, and your country and browser
        family. Visits are grouped with a code derived from your IP address and
        browser, which is scrambled and changes every day. Your IP address itself is not stored.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, which reports totals such as page
        views, referrers and device types.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Nothing is sold, used for ads, or used to track you across other sites.</p>
    <h2>Purchases and email</h2>
    <p>
      Purchases are handled by Gumroad, under
      <a href="https://gumroad.com/privacy">Gumroad's privacy policy</a>. I receive
      your email address and what you bought, and use it only to deliver and
      support the purchase. If you email me, I keep the conversation so I can reply.
    </p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you can ask what I hold about you and have it deleted. Email
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Data controller:
      {site.business}, {site.location}.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated 19 September 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Page>
